{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature for network response variability temperature for network response variability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","fileName":"Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature for Network Response Variability","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering","Top-P for Network Response Diversity","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature for network response variability temperature for network response variability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","fileName":"Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature for Network Response Variability","heading":"Temperature for Network Response Variability","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Temperature changes how strongly a language model favors its most likely next tokens. Raising it produces more varied responses; lowering it tends to produce more repeatable ones. It is a generation control, not a confidence score and not a factuality guarantee.\n\nNetwork configuration and diagnostic tasks usually benefit from low variability because command syntax and ordered procedures leave little room for creative alternatives. Higher values may help brainstorming, but extreme settings can make even a familiar VLAN request incoherent. Temperature should be set together with [[Top-P for Network Response Diversity]] and tested on the actual task.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering","Top-P for Network Response Diversity","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"temperature for network response variability temperature for network response variability","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","fileName":"Temperature for Network Response Variability.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Temperature for Network Response Variability","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[ainetworkingcookbook.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Model and Prompt Engineering","Top-P for Network Response Diversity","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}